!!
!! This is the GAS PHASE CHEMISTRY INPUT DECK for ASP		
!! that is read in by SetGasPhaseChemistry() in GasPhaseChemistry.h
!!
!! The following is the full list of gases tracked in the gas phase 
!! (water vapor is hard coded in and should not be included here)
!!
!! Specify the following variables; separating each by a semi-colon and 
!! including each on a single line for each gas:
!!	NAME (no more than 15 characters): Make sure this is the same
!!	     as that used in the other chemical input decks
!!	CONSTANT?: Some chemicals will be held fixed, and others allowed
!!	  to evolve with time.  Put a 1 if evolving, 0 if not
!!  PEROXY RADICAL?: 2 if should be included in RO2_T and RCO3_T sums (acyl peroxy),
!!                         1 if should be included in RO2_T sum only, 0 if not
!!	MOLECULAR MASS (g / mole)
!!	FIRE EMISSION FACTOR (g per kg dry matter burned) 
!!	BACKGROUND CONCENTRATION (ppbv)
!!	DEPOSITION VELOCITY (cm/s)
!!
!! INITIAL CONCENTRATION FLAG AND VALUE:
!! First (integer) flag is:
!! 0 if initial concentrations should be calculated from Emission factor
!! 1 if initial concentrations should be set to a negligible value, as in STILT
!! 2 if initial concentrations should be read in from the emission factor slot 
!! (to have back-compatability with older input files of ASP v2.1 and earlier)
!! Second value is the initial CO concentration in ppbv to be used in the calculation of other initial values from the Emission Factors
2; 1700!   !! Flag 2 = initial concentrations (ppbv) are read from the 5th column below; second value is the initial CO (ppbv)
!!
!!
!! Use the same name here as in the aerosol chemistry input deck to 
!! assure proper matching between the two
!! Put CO first to use gasphasechems_scale.pro;Evolve flag;Peroxy Flag;MW;Init Conc;Back Conc;Dep Vel!;;;
